   <text type="letter">
      
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener>
               <salute>My dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">friends</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>The War Aims arrived this morning and I read them immediately. They are excellent,
               excellent, excellent. I shall use my energy to make them known in my circle of
               friends and acquaintances. Tonight will be the monthly dinner of the <q>Fireside
                  Friends,</q> a very potential group of younger (25-55 <add place="sublinear"><hi
                     rend="hand">years of age</hi></add>) prominent Quakers, <add place="sublinear"
                     ><hi rend="hand">including Federal Judge + College President.</hi></add> I
               shall distribute the booklets there. -- Wish I had 100 copies, hope you get them in
               millions of issues, they ought to be in every contemporary&apos;s hand and memory. I
               am going to mail one to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4597" type="person">Harry
                  Wright</rs>, City College, with an extra letter.</p>
            <p>Man fühlt jetzt endlich, dass der Kreis sich schliesst, – der geistige, dessen, was wir alle erlebt haben
            und was so schwer zu deuten war. Wunderbar und klar und richtig gesehen und ausgedrueckt, Sie verdienen
            wirklich grossen Dank und Anerkennung Aller dafuer.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Gruesse</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4596" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Fridel Stoetzner.</hi></rs></signed>
               <dateline><date when="1942-04-24">April 24, 1942.</date></dateline></closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
